A||||13||batboy||Mad at my Fiero too||||1||
Z||000000||batboy||06-07-2000||10:36 PM||||I finally got fed up with my 85 GT making all kinds of noise. I have an exhaust manifold leaking. The shocks and struts are all leaking fluid so they squeak and bounce, the end links on the sway bars are shot so they rattle on every little bump, and the latest is the rear brake pads on one side reached the wear indicator so it's screeching. Went to the parts store and bought end links and a set of rear pads (going to use the old shocks and struts I took off the Batmobile because they don't have very many miles on them and are still in good shape).<P>Got home tonight and whipped off the front tires. Decided to see how much I could get done in one evening. The metal spacer sleeve on one side of the sway bar end link was rusted solid to the long bolt. I think, no problem and fetched up the penetrating oil and a bigger hammer. I let it soak and change out the shocks. The decide to be a little stubborn and time consuming too. After working up a sweat and getting a little annoyed, I finally get the shocks off (they look like originals and this car has nearly 150k miles).<P>Back to beating and chiseling on the end link. It don't budge. I get pissed and start cussing. It must of looked like that movie "A Christmas Story" where Ralphie is swearing up a storm while he's beating up the bully. I'm hammering away uttering a nonstop string of profanity. Finally I throw down my tools in a fit of rage.<P>I go fetch every extention cord I own and string it out to the driveway. Time for the power tools! I select my Makita 4" angle grinder and go to town. Sparks are flying everywhere. Molten pieces of the end link nut and bolt drip to the driveway. The rubber catches on fire, but I don't give a bat's guano. I keep grinding away until it falls apart. I turn off my smoking hot grinder and exclaim out loud, "There, that'll teach ya, you son-of-a-b!tch!"<P>Suddenly I heard loud laughter behind me. My neighbor had walked up behind me and had been watching for I don't know how long. Boy was my face red. He had two beers in his hand and offered me one. Wow, thanks! I needed that! Boy, am I glad I don't have to wrench for a living. When it ceases to be fun, it's nice to be able to put the tools up and leave the rest for another time. One happy note, I found my 10mm socket that's been missing for a couple months.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Dan86gt3.8||06-07-2000||11:39 PM||||hell yeah I know what you mean batboy!  When I had my 3.8 out a couple weeks ago I snapped 2 manifold bolts in half so they were still stuck in the nuts that were tach welded to the flange well after about half a can of rust remover we had to take the manifold comp[letely off the engine go put it in a vice and with one hit with a chissel and hammer the tach welds let go and off came the nut.  A long way to go for some stupid rust!  We tried everyting to I even had the air grinder out but it didn't do anything except give me less bolt to grab onto!  Anyways a hammer and some love taps sole just about everything! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||06-08-2000||02:54 AM||||Batboy, I know excatly what you mean! It's funny now but when things don't go easy usually tools are flying and the colorful metafores are echoing!||||reg||12
Z||000003||Raydar||06-08-2000||11:24 AM||||Was in my basement/garage. Got mad at something (don't even remember what).<BR>Threw my keyring. <BR>Bad move.<BR>Took me *forever* to find my keys, in all the clutter. <BR>||||reg||11
Z||000004||lennyb4||06-08-2000||11:30 AM||||Me and my wife had to go downtown about three summers ago. Well the building we went to was right next to a bridge that overlooks the cuyahoga river. When we came back out i had a ticket, needless to say i got pissed off started b**ching and complaining and ended up throwing my keys (car, work, house, etc) as hard as i could. Well as it turns out in my little fit of rage i threw them clear off the bridge.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> Talk about feeling stupid. We still laugh about it till this day.. ||||reg||4
Z||000005||FieroGT||06-08-2000||01:35 PM||||Batboy, it seems like working on the car when something isn't going right is the only thing that has the power to really piss me of and cause a fit of rage. My friends already know this and have held me back and taken the 4 lb. hammer outof my hand before I could do some kind of irrational damage. <P>I'm really OK most of the time, it just seems that some things on the Fiero (or whatever I happen to be working on at the time) can really get to me....<P><BR>John||||reg||1
Z||000006||BlackGT||06-08-2000||01:55 PM||||Hey BatBoy,<P> I scream out loud with laughter everytime I read one of your posts or comments on this forum! You crack me up...but I truly feel your pain Dude! I spent 3 1/2 days cussin while underneath my 86GT changing my clutch <BR>in my friends garage while his wife listened<BR>to the string of obscenities escaping my lips! All she could hear were the very colorful words I used and see my feet sticking out from underneath my car. If I didn`t love this go kart so much I wouldn`t<BR>have done it but like everyone else on this<BR>forum these cars are a labor of love for us and I for one don`t drive anything else!!! <BR>||||reg||6
Z||000007||MotherGoose||06-08-2000||01:57 PM||||My neighbor did the same thing day before yesterday.  I was working on my fiero when things weren't going right, I through my tool box about twenty feet.  He happened to be driving up when this happened.  As he was walking over I was cussing like "Raulphies" dad with the furnace.  He said, "I think you need this."  I slammed the beer and started laughing at how stupid I was being.||||reg||1
Z||000008||tgowens||06-08-2000||01:57 PM||||Batboy, you should have been a writer instead of a mechanic!! - that story was a hoot!!! (but then you never <I>said</I> you were a mechanic, did ya??<P>(by the way, you all <I>do</I> know that you have to use a <B>metric</B> hammer on the Fiero, don't you??????)||||reg||1
Z||000009||batboy||06-08-2000||03:19 PM||||Nope, I'm not a mechanic nor an author, but that don't stop me from wrenchin' or writin'. I've actually had quite a number of articles published, mainly technical papers on karst geology or caving. I've done a couple fictional short stories too. Maybe I'll post my favorite in the off topic section, I promise it's short, easy to read, and fun. Lots of people don't seem to appreciate my dry sense of humor, but some of you guys are apparently warped enough to like it.||||reg||1
Z||000010||lennyb4||06-08-2000||03:28 PM||||Hey Bats..You go caving? Man its soooo hard to find other people into it. Once your deep into that cave it just seems like another world. Found one last year in our state park, not to bad about a hundred foot repel in then goes on for about 1/2 mile w/little crevisways leading off in various directions. Did some soft foot exploration but nothing spectacular.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||4
Z||000011||tgowens||06-08-2000||04:41 PM||||and I was out drivin' Lenny's Fiero while he was in the cave!!! hahaha||||reg||1
Z||000012||batboy||06-08-2000||06:03 PM||||Yep, I'm a caver. Been doing it hardcore since 1984...although slowing down some in the last few years. I visited my first wild cave back in 1977, but actually fell in love with caves as a kid when our family took one of those commercial cave tours in the Black Hills while on vacation. My master's thesis was on karst geology and cave development in the Flint Hills of Kansas. If you found a 100 foot drop and a 1/2 mile long cave in Ohio, send me an email. I know several Ohio cavers and none of them know anything about a cave that extensive. I'm guessing this was in Indiana or Kentucky, maybe? Remember to always wear a helmet, take at least 3 sources of light, and never go caving alone. I've been on cave rescues before, including a double fatality, involving inexperienced and unprepared novices. The caver motto is: Take nothing but pictures, leave nothing but footprints, kill nothing but time. This is why I have my nickname...I like bats!||||reg||1
Z||000013||turbo86se||06-09-2000||09:50 AM||||Hey bats! <BR>When I was younger, my parents dropped me off at a summer camp for a few weeks, one for one week I went caving in Pennslyvania. It was awesome!!!  The one cave I remember was called Hamilton. There was a really cool clay room that everyone made little figurines out of clay, several wind tunnels, lots of water to swim through and at one point we had to swim under a boulder to get to the other side. One thing I clearly remember is crawling through a narrow passageway into a large room with a high ceiling.  My friend and I smelled something and heard strange sounds. We shined our flashlights straight up at the ceiling and saw thousands and thousands of bats! It was very cool!!!!<BR>Someday I'll do this again,  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
